285
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:51,150
Just toss them underhand.

286
00:11:51,150 --> 00:11:52,950
Nice and gentle. Nice and calm.

287
00:11:52,950 --> 00:11:55,620
A big overhand throw can scare them, right?

288
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:57,960
(Waiting)

289
00:11:58,320 --> 00:11:59,560
It's waiting. How cute.

290
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:00,620
There you go.

291
00:12:01,090 --> 00:12:03,360
It's so pretty. The one behind is really pretty too, right?

292
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:06,330
The one behind is really pretty. Oh, my.

293
00:12:08,630 --> 00:12:09,970
Oh, they can catch it.

294
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:13,500
You know, like normal dogs, like German Shepherds.

295
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:15,410
- These guys are strong, right?
- I'm sure.

296
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:17,940
What if they go against a wolf?

297
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:19,480
- The wolf would win.
- The wolf?

298
