- Good boy.

323
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:18,770
They look like Huskies you can easily see.

324
00:13:18,770 --> 00:13:20,300
Right? If we weren't told,

325
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,370
I'd think they were normal dogs you see around Canada.

326
00:13:22,370 --> 00:13:23,370
Right?

327
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:27,080
Oh, goodness.

328
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:29,010
(They enter the cage feeling much more comfortable.)

329
00:13:29,510 --> 00:13:31,220
They're so pretty.

330
00:13:31,850 --> 00:13:33,620
Because they're low-content.

331
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:38,120
(A beautiful odd-eyed wolfdog)

332
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:39,420
They're so adorable.

333
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:40,420
So pretty.

334
00:13:42,130 --> 00:13:43,560
They're really like dogs.

335
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:45,060
That's the perfect way to put it.

336
00:13:46,460 --> 00:13:47,530
Hi.

337
00:13:48,130 --> 00:13:49,130
- They're coming up to us.
- So cute.

338
00:13:49,130 --> 00:13:50,700
- So pretty.
- Good boy.

339
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:53,270
- So cute.
- They like people.

340
00:13:54,510 --> 00:13:55,610
(What is this?)

341
00:13:57,610 --> 00:14:01,280
(These wolfdogs are so mischievous and full of curiosity.)

342
00:14:01,650 --> 00:14:03,980
Again, these guys are a lot more interested...

343
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:05,720
